    scenario:{chapter:3,sourceText:'I put my hand on the red door instead of the green button.',instruction:'Have Noor tell Dax the whole plan before he crosses, so he chooses to stay without being shamed into it.',rewriteText:'I called Dax back before the fire door closed.\n\n“I need someone to hold a shield for people who cannot respawn. You get to say no.”\n\nHe looked at the grey icon over his own head. Then at Bea.\n\n“What happens to your class?”\n\n“I lose the room.”\n\nDax set his sword on the floor. “Then we build another one.”',continueText:'Arlo knelt beside the map. Dax held its corners while Tess tore clean strips from her apron. Nobody had assigned roles. They were simply doing the next useful thing.\n\nThe Auditor watched, waiting for a party leader to issue an order. None came.',whatIfText:'Noor discloses the cost early. Dax stays by choice, giving Arlo time to prepare the circuit before the Auditor intervenes. Trust improves, but the loss of safe-room protection remains real.',futureText:'The camp had a second doorway now. Dax built it too wide, and Arlo complained until a woman arrived carrying an injured man between two poles.\n\nThey fitted through without turning him sideways.\n\nNoor hung the old shield above the lintel. On its back, Bea had painted four words: THERE IS ROOM HERE.',bridge:'An informed decision keeps Dax inside; extra preparation shortens the transfer; Noor still loses system protection; the party builds a camp that can take stretchers.',titles:{rewrite:'Ask before the door closes',continue_block:'No party leader required',what_if:'What if Dax chooses to stay?',future_jump:'A door wide enough',roleplay_session:'One respawn, five people'},delta:{before:'A conditional alliance',after:'A freely chosen commitment',description:'Dax knows the risk before agreeing; Noor no longer has to trade shame for cooperation.'},roleplay:{opening:'The transfer may cost your last life. I need you to know that before you decide to hold the shield.',reply:'I appreciate the warning. Most recruitment speeches leave out the dying. Show me where to stand, and tell me when I can still change my mind.',narration:'Dax turns the grey respawn token between his fingers. It no longer looks like a medal.',responses:['I have one life left. So do they. I think I kept forgetting the second part.','Tell Arlo I can hold the shield. Tell him to explain the wire slowly. I am considerably better at posing than electrical work.','When we get outside, you are resting. That is not a party-leader order. It is a request from somebody who would like to keep knowing you.']},alternative:{title:'What if Noor takes the combat respec?',instruction:'Give Noor an easier personal escape that permanently closes the transfer route for the locals.',text:'The respec window promised a sword and a clean exit. Noor’s finger hovered over it. Behind the glass, Bea practised writing her own name on a fogged patch. The offer had a countdown. The people it excluded did not get one.'}},
